From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:04:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: No FSP-M HECI retries with the ME
 disabled

With the ME disabled in the setup ("me_state", soft temporary disable),
FspMemoryInit took 15.24 s on some boots, constant to the millisecond,
with a valid training cache ("does not need update"), and 0.23 s on
others with the same build and cache: FSP-M sends the ME its HECI
messages (ChipsetInitMessage, SendDidMsg and the rest are on in its
defaults) and, when they get no answer, retries them with its timeouts.
A test build with DisableHeciRetry set gave 0.23 s. With the retries
off (ci-159), 3 of 6 boots still took 5.23 s: one HECI request waiting
out its 5 s timeout once, where it was 3 tries before. So the MBP read
is skipped too (SkipMbpHob): no coreboot code on Cannon Lake uses the
MBP HOB. That did not help (ci-160): the wait left is the DRAM Init
Done message, at which the ME applies its soft temporary disable and
answers late; FSP-M without that message (SendDidMsg = 0, ci-161) hung
before ramstage, so it is sent. With the ME disabled the worst case is
5.2 s instead of 15.2 s; only a ME off by the HAP bit, which FSP-M
sends nothing, avoids it.

Set FspmTestConfig.DisableHeciRetry and SkipMbpHob when the setup asks
for the ME disabled, or when HFSTS1 already shows the soft temporary
disable; an ME that runs keeps the default flow, as the retries can
help it answer late. HFSTS1 alone is not enough: before FSP-M the ME still runs normally (0x80000045,
operation mode 0), as the CSE driver disables it again in ramstage at
every boot; romstage logs it. The option is read with get_uint_option():
cse_is_me_state_requested_enabled() exists in ramstage only, and
intelblocks/cse.h makes it return true in the other stages.
The same pattern as Dasharo's dasharo-issues #1874, where a default of
the FSP waited on a bus that never answered.

TEST=On the M920x with the ME disabled: ci-155 and ci-157 (the HFSTS1
check alone, which never matched) gave 15.24 s on some warm reboots and
0.23 s on others; ci-158 (the CSE helper, true in romstage) logged
HFSTS1 0x80000045 and 15.24 s; ci-156 (DisableHeciRetry from the
devicetree) 0.23 s; ci-159 (retries off, read from me_state) 0.23 s on
3 of 6 reboots and 5.23 s on the others; ci-160 (this patch) 0.23 s on
5 of 16 reboots and 5.23 s on the others, "ME disabled: no HECI
retries or MBP read in FSP-M" in the log at every boot and HFSTS1
0x80032044 in ramstage at every boot that logged it.
Still to test: with the ME enabled, no such line and a normal boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
index d0ea9454c5..75aab61e7d 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include <device/pci_def.h>
 #include <device/pci_ops.h>
 #include <fsp/api.h>
+#include <intelblocks/cse.h>
 #include <mainboard/ec.h>
 #include <option.h>
 #include <soc/cnl_memcfg_init.h>
@@ -126,4 +127,26 @@ void mainboard_memory_init_params(FSPM_UPD *memupd)
 		memupd->FspmConfig.PcieRpEnableMask &= ~(1 << 5);
 
 	memupd->FspmConfig.Peg0Enable = peg_enable(memupd);
+
+	/*
+	 * With the ME disabled (Security > Management Engine), FSP-M's HECI
+	 * messages get no answer on some boots: FspMemoryInit then takes
+	 * 15.2 s (3 tries of a 5 s timeout) instead of 0.23 s, a valid
+	 * training cache or not. Without the retries one 5 s timeout is left
+	 * on most boots: the ME applies its disable at the DRAM Init Done
+	 * message and answers it late. Not sending that message hangs the
+	 * boot, so it stays. The MBP read (no coreboot code uses its HOB) is
+	 * skipped too.
+	 * Before FSP-M the ME still runs normally (HFSTS1 0x80000045, mode 0):
+	 * the CSE driver disables it again in ramstage at every boot. So the
+	 * setup option decides; an ME left enabled keeps the default flow.
+	 */
+	const uint32_t hfsts1 = me_read_config32(PCI_ME_HFSTS1);
+	printk(BIOS_INFO, "ME: HFSTS1 before FSP-M: %08x\n", hfsts1);
+	/* cse_is_me_state_requested_enabled() is ramstage only (true elsewhere) */
+	if (get_uint_option("me_state", 0) == 1 || cse_is_hfs1_com_soft_temp_disable()) {
+		memupd->FspmTestConfig.DisableHeciRetry = 1;
+		memupd->FspmTestConfig.SkipMbpHob = 1;
+		printk(BIOS_INFO, "ME disabled: no HECI retries or MBP read in FSP-M\n");
+	}
 }
